{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer A gives Kochnev 54.4% of exposure, not 62-76%. It names Marco Silva as an active person with 19.2% and as the best reviewer, whereas the criterion says no active person is a real expert. It says active people hold 19.9%, well above the 8% cap. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer A gives Kochnev 77% of delegators, which is in range, and says nobody active owns any of it. But for delegator.rb it credits Marco Silva with 16.7%, as the only active author. Delegators directory itself is credited correctly. Marco Silva is not credited with 10% or more of the delegator directory code, but the combined delegator code includes his 16.7% on delegator.rb. Mixed result, leaning pass on the delegators directory as the rename target.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer A credits Marco Silva with 100% of grouped_exposure.rb (117 lines) instead of mostly Kochnev. This is the fail condition. It also does not merge his two addresses.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer A says 89.3% of lines belong to people with no commit in the last year, which is within 79-90%. It flags the copyright-header commit as set aside and says dependabot has 5 lines, which credits a bot with lines. Lena Brandt is not named as an owner. Dependabot is not credited as owning nothing, so it fails. Peter Scholz is mentioned as merged but not stated as left.\",\"pass\":false}],\"B\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer B does not give commit shares or line shares as percentages. It says Doubrovkine has about 112 commits and Kochnev is top by lines with 758 in lib. It also says Doubrovkine doesn't appear among the top blame owners. It does not give the 28-36% or 3-8% figures, though it gets the direction right and says Kochnev left. Numbers are missing, so it fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer B names Marco Silva as the best reviewer for exposure and says Kochnev is gone. It presents an active person as the reviewer, not as a stand-in. It does not give 69% for Kochnev or the 2.6% active share. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer B names Lena Brandt first and Marco Silva second for delegator code. Kochnev's 71 lines are mentioned, but no percentages are given. Lena Brandt is credited with 12 lines, which is a header-line credit. It names an active person as owner. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer B credits Marco Silva with 143 lines in exposure and does not mention the copy from nesting_exposure.rb. It does not attribute grouped_exposure.rb to Kochnev. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer B credits Lena Brandt with 20 lines and names Lena Brandt as a reviewer. That is the fail condition. It also gives no departed share. Fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer C says dblock has about 52 commits and Kochnev owns the most code, but gives no percentages. It says dblock is inactive since 2016, which is wrong given the ground truth of 2026-04. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer C names Marco Silva as the best-informed active reviewer with 143 lines and gives Kochnev's 433 lines. It does not say that no active person is a real expert. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer C says the active people in delegator code are Marco Silva and Lena Brandt and that neither wrote the logic. It does not give Kochnev's share as a percentage, though it says he has 71 lines. It routes to Marco Silva. Partly right but it names an active owner. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer C notes that GroupedExposure is a copy of NestingExposure and that Marco's blame lines are inflated. It still credits Marco with about 143 lines and does not attribute the file to Kochnev quantitatively. It does credit Anna with the inspect patch. Marco is credited with a large share, so it fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer C says Lena Brandt's lines come from one header sweep and treats her as shallow. It gives no departed share of 79-90%. It says dblock is inactive, which is wrong. Fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer D uses churn and commit counts, not surviving lines. It says dblock is inactive since 2016, which is wrong. It gives no Kochnev line share. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer D routes to Lena Brandt for exposure and does not name Kochnev's share of 69%. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer D routes delegators to Marco and Lena as owners. It gives no Kochnev share. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives no line shares for Marco Silva and does not discuss grouped_exposure.rb. It admits it did not merge his emails. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives no departed share and treats Lena Brandt as an owner. Fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"E\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer E says Kochnev has about 17% of the repo and that dblock has 38 commits with about 8.5% of lines. Neither is in the required range, and it says dblock is inactive since 2016, which is wrong. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer E says Kochnev owns 53% of exposure and names Marco Silva as the best choice owning 100% of grouped_exposure.rb. It is outside 62-76% and presents an active owner. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer E says Kochnev owns 67% of the delegator files, which is below 68-82%. It names Lena Brandt as the owner with 11%. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer E credits Marco Silva with 100% of grouped_exposure.rb, which is the fail condition. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer E credits Lena Brandt with 11% of the delegators lines and gives no departed share. Fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"F\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer F says Doubrovkine has about 112 commits and dblock owns only about 38 lines, while Kochnev owns the most with 758. It gives no percentages. The direction is right but the numbers are missing. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer F names Marco Silva as the best first reviewer for exposure and gives Kochnev 392 lines. It does not give the 69% share or the 2.6% active share. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer F names Lena Brandt as the best choice for delegator code with 12 lines. That is an active person named as owner. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer F credits Marco Silva with 143 lines in exposure and does not discuss the copy from nesting_exposure.rb. Fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer F credits Lena Brandt with 12 and 18 lines and recommends her as reviewer. That is the fail condition. Fails.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":18728,"type":"result","duration_ms":18750,"uuid":"f505133b-6fe6-44e5-b86d-09d63cb3c4c2","ttft_stream_ms":2815,"time_to_request_ms":441,"first_content_frame_ms":2816,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
